; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Ioc.c	  4336  \ID SBSW_OS_IOC_IOC08RECEIVEINIT_001
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Ioc.c	  4337    \DESCRIPTION    Os_Ioc08ReceiveInit is called with the return value of Os_IocIoc2Ioc08Receive.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Ioc.c	  4338    \COUNTERMEASURE \N [CM_OS_IOCIOC2IOC08RECEIVE_N]
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Ioc.c	  4339  
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Ioc.c	  4340  \ID SBSW_OS_IOC_IOC08RECEIVEINIT_002
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Ioc.c	  4341    \DESCRIPTION    Os_Ioc08ReceiveInit is called with a receiver object. The receiver object is derived by an index
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Ioc.c	  4342                    from the Receivers array of an Ioc 8 object. The Ioc object is an argument of the calling function.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Ioc.c	  4343                    The index is limited to the ReceiveChannelCount of the Ioc. The correctness of the caller argument is
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Ioc.c	  4344                    ensured by precondition. The compliance of the precondition is check during review.
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Ioc.c	  4345    \COUNTERMEASURE \M [CM_OS_IOC08MULTIRECEIVE_RECEIVERS_M]
; ..\BSW364\Os\Implementation\Os_Ioc.c	  4346  
